WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.570
My phone is newer than my brother's.

2
00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:05.720
English needs just an apostrophe and an S.

3
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.150
French has no apostrophe S.

4
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.720
So do you say «le téléphone
de mon frère» all over again?

5
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.020
Essays get worse: the latter,

6
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.220
the former, some people, others.

7
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:22.100
Yet French writers argue both
sides without naming anyone.

8
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.440
How does French pull that off
without repeating the noun?

9
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.150
In this mission, you'll
cross out a repeated noun

10
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:30.200
and see what takes its place.

11
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.410
Then you'll switch owners in the lab:

12
00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:34.950
«la voiture de Paul», «les livres de Léa».

13
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:38.200
Your mission: find out
how French says mine,

14
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.960
the latter and some people,

15
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.870
without ever repeating the noun.
